# Naming Conventions

## File Names (snake_case)

| Type | Suffix | Example |
|------|--------|---------|
| Page | `_page` | `login_page.dart` |
| Cubit | `_cubit` | `login_cubit.dart` |
| State | `_state` | `login_state.dart` |
| Model | `_model` | `user_model.dart` |
| Repository | `_repository` | `auth_repository.dart` |
| Service | `_service` | `secure_storage_service.dart` |
| Implementation | `_impl` | `secure_storage_service_impl.dart` |
| Interceptor | `_interceptor` | `auth_interceptor.dart` |
| Guard | `_guard` | `auth_guard.dart` |
| Global widget | `app_` prefix | `app_button.dart` |
| Mock | `mock_` prefix | `mock_auth_repository.dart` |

## Class Names (PascalCase)

- Suffix must match file type: `LoginPage`, `LoginCubit`, `LoginState`, `UserModel`
- Interfaces: plain name (`AuthRepository`). Implementations: add `Impl` (`AuthRepositoryImpl`) or tech prefix (`SharedPrefLocalStorageServiceImpl`)
- Global widgets: `App` prefix (`AppButton`, `AppTextField`, `AppSnackbar`)
- Generated route classes: `<PageName>Route` (auto-generated, e.g. `LoginRoute`)

## Never

- Never use abbreviations in file/class names (use `authentication`, not `auth_svc`)
- Never mix naming patterns within the same layer
